From: Surface Pro X port
Subject: [PATCH] ipa: libipa: Match OV5693 whole-unit analogue gain controls

The mainline driver exposes gain 1..127, shifts it left by four before
writing 0x350a, and shifts right by four on readback. Its V4L2 control is
already in whole gain units, not the register's fixed-point representation.
Dividing it by 16 reports unity gain as 0.0625 and requests a gain code
sixteen times too large. Keep black level unchanged (RAW10 level 16).

--- a/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
+++ b/src/ipa/libipa/camera_sensor_helper.cpp
@@ -776,7 +776,7 @@ public:
 	CameraSensorHelperOv5693()
 	{
 		blackLevel_ = 1024;
-		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 16 };
+		gain_ = AnalogueGainLinear{ 1, 0, 0, 1 };
 	}
 };
 REGISTER_CAMERA_SENSOR_HELPER("ov5693", CameraSensorHelperOv5693)
